ortcut, a track of its own with `surface: 'dirt'`, leaves and rejoins); karts are `world.vehicle({ kind: 'kart', rig })` raced by `E.Race` (`race.update(dt, null)`: laps, places, its drivers, items); the camera `'behind'` each; set a kart that has left the course back on the road after a moment (Lakitu); two players through `game.splitScreen(2)` and `world.addCamera`.\n165:**Rail shooter (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon).** The 3D FLIGHT kit. The ship is a `world.flyer({ rail: { path, speed, w, h } })`: the rail's point rides on and the ship moves in a window across it; the camera `'behind'` follows the rail's point (`f.frame`), not the ship. Waves of foes live in the rail's frame (a distance along it and an offset across), so they keep up; a roll (`f.rolling`) turns shots aside; a held fire charges a shot that locks on (`f.seek`); at the end, `f.o.rail = null` and `bounds` give free flight round a boss. A wingman talks on `Dialog`'s radio (`modal: false`).\n167:**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n172:**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes over a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell; each step and quarter turn is a tween, so the view glides. Gates are `world.thing('door')`s that rise (`world.unlock` for one with a key); the monsters walk an `E.Grid` cell to cell; `E.Fog` keeps what the party has seen for the automap; `E.Turns` in `'atb'` is real time (Dungeon Master), in `'speed'` the dungeon waits for the party (Wizardry). The party's portraits sit under the view (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n174:**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n176:- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n178:**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n183:**Gauntlet.** Start from the ADVENTURE slice (a `TileMap` dungeon in `threequarter` or `topdown`).\n187:**Frogger.** An `E.Grid` of lanes in `overhead`: the frog an `E.GridMover` that hops a cell per press; each lane a row of cars or logs moving at its own speed (`x += v * dt`, wrapping at the screen's edge). On a road a car's box kills; on the river the frog rides a log (add its speed) and drowns off one. Five homes at the top; a clock bar per life.\n189:**Sokoban.** An `E.Grid` from text rows (`#` walls, `$` crates, `.` goals, `@` you); you an `E.GridMover` with `push(cx, cy, dx, dy)` that moves a crate when the cell beyond is free; won when every goal has a crate. Keep each move's state for undo (Backspace) and a reset; count moves and pushes.\n191:**Sonic without the loops (Sonic the Hedgehog's speed on flat ground and slopes).** Start from the PLATFORMER slice: `new E.Platformer({ momentum: true })` (speed builds up and carries, slowing on the way up a slope and gathering on the way down: tiles of `kind: 'slope'`), a roll on down at speed, rings that scatter when hit (`E.Bullets` fired with `grav`) and are lost after a while, springs and long camera leads (`game.follow(hero, { lead: 60 })`). Loops and walls run round need a ground of any angle the Platformer doesn't have: leave them out.\n193:**Cinematic platformer (Prince of Persia, Flashback, Another World).** Start from the PLATFORMER slice with `new E.Platformer({ ledge: true, crouch: true })`: a step is a fixed distance, a jump a fixed arc (no control in the air), a ledge grabbed and climbed in steps, a run that needs room to stop. Screens one at a time (`game.cam.room`), each a room of the rooms module's `E.World`. Animation is the point: the Humanoid's moves at their full key poses, or a mocap clip (`docs/MOCAP.md`) for the climb and the fall; a sword fight is an `E.Fighter` pair from the fight module, in the side view.\n195:**Light guns (Time Crisis, The House of the Dead, Virtua Cop).** Start from the 3D FLIGHT slice's rails (or a 2D screen of `overhead` sprites): the camera rides an `E.Path` (`world.camera` following the rail's point), foes pop out from behind cover on a script by distance, and the player aims with the pointer: a click (a tap on a phone) at `input.pointer()` hits the nearest foe whose `world.project(x, y, z)` point lies within its size on the screen of it and that the camera sees (`world.clear` from the camera's pose); the reticle is drawn at the pointer. Reload by shooting off the screen (or a button); a pedal to take cover (a button that lowers the camera behind cover). Each enemy's shot is telegraphed by a ring that closes.\n197:**Indoor corridor shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007) on the 3D engine.** Start from the 3D SHOOTER slice's first person: its gun, hitscan (`world.ray`), recoil and hit markers, with a level of text instead of its terrain (`level: { rows }`: corridors of walls, doors that slide or swing, `world.thing('door', ...)` with `locked: 'red'` and keys, lifts as platforms). Monsters are mobs that walk the level's flow field toward you and fire when `world.clear` says they see you; the camera is `'fixed'` with `capture: true`, turned by `camera.takeMouse()`. GoldenEye adds aiming down the sights (the overlay's fov) and guards that react to where they are shot.\n199:**Mash-ups.** The kits don't depend on each other. Some examples:\n202:- a brawler with bullet-hell bosses: `Bullets` with the `'ground'` plane;","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UuH7T1o75PtmQGsirHg8AW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggySRJwwyabWDCcJzHcg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017GeNkfS2GraaLCKQRz7iLT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/plan-xe9c1ea-engine.Yt57/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && awk 'NR>=402 && NR<=606' AI_GUIDE.md | sed -n '31,36p;49,54p;167,171p;199,205p'; echo ----; sed -n 606,700p AI_GUIDE.md","description":"Read brawler, arcade, sports recipes and big-game lessons"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5143,"cache_read_input_tokens":131057,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5143},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"12141bce-6b8f-4626-a762-28db1b61b638","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:14.211Z","request_id":"req_011CggySR548FhPMEx3UP4Dq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017GeNkfS2GraaLCKQRz7iLT":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/plan-xe9c1ea-engine.Yt57/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && awk 'NR>=402 && NR<=606' AI_GUIDE.md | sed -n '31,36p;49,54p;167,171p;199,205p'; echo ----; sed -n 606,700p AI_GUIDE.md","description":"Read brawler, arcade, sports recipes and big-game lessons"}}}
