{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PHuNBw9p5ba56YtxhtzQnC","type":"tool_result","content":"- `body.step = 2`: the height it walks up without jumping (E.HEIGHTS.step)\n- `body.vx = 0`, `body.vy = 0`, `body.vz = 0`: its speed, world units per second\n- `body.x = 0`, `body.y = 0`, `body.z = 0`: its position (z = feet)\n\n## 17b. Actions\n\n- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n- `action.canCancel` †: true during a beat marked as one the action may be cut short in (spec.cancel)\n- `action.cancel()` †: stop now: the bodies stay where they are\n- `action.invulnerable` †: true while hits should miss (spec.safe: [from, to] of the action's progress)\n- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n- `action.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state for the body (merge extra over it): x, y, z, its speed, facing and the beat's pose\n- `action.u` †: 0..1 through the whole action\n- `action.update(dt)` †: move the bodies one step; returns true while the action runs (false once it has ended)\n- `action.beat` †: the name of the beat playing now\n- `action.beats` †: [[name, seconds], ...]\n- `action.body`, `action.other` †: the bodies it moves\n- `action.done = false` †: it has ended (or was cancelled)\n- `action.duration` †: the action's length in seconds (o.speed shortens it)\n- `action.name` †: the action's name\n- `action.o` †: the options it was given\n- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n- `action.start` †: where the body was when it began\n- `action.t = 0` †: seconds played\n\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a tween or script (until it is done), a generator (run as a script of its own, and waited for), E.all([...]) or E.any([...]) (each of these). It runs at once to its first yield. Cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials, attract modes. Returns the Script\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"20d8f310-d589-4206-9d44-3e82a2fbbfe3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:08.164Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `body.step = 2`: the height it walks up without jumping (E.HEIGHTS.step)\n- `body.vx = 0`, `body.vy = 0`, `body.vz = 0`: its speed, world units per second\n- `body.x = 0`, `body.y = 0`, `body.z = 0`: its position (z = feet)\n\n## 17b. Actions\n\n- `E.ACTIONS: climbUp, climbJump, vault, hopDown, roll, getUp, takedown` †: the actions E.Action plays. Add your own: E.ACTIONS.name = { beats, setup, at }; setup(A) and at(A, beat, u) get the action: its options A.o, A.start (where the body began), A.body; setup may change A.beats. Play one: mover.play('takedown', { other })\n- `new E.Action(name, o = {}) → action`: new E.Action(name, { body, to, other, dir, dist, top, aerial, reverse, speed: 1 }): play E.ACTIONS[name] on a body (and on o.other for a paired action). It moves them itself: run update(dt) every step instead of their physics, and feed rigState() to the rig. Each body ends standing where the action put it\n- `action.canCancel` †: true during a beat marked as one the action may be cut short in (spec.cancel)\n- `action.cancel()` †: stop now: the bodies stay where they are\n- `action.invulnerable` †: true while hits should miss (spec.safe: [from, to] of the action's progress)\n- `action.otherState(extra)` †: the rig state for the other body of a paired action (the victim of a takedown)\n- `action.rigState(extra)` †: the rig state for the body (merge extra over it): x, y, z, its speed, facing and the beat's pose\n- `action.u` †: 0..1 through the whole action\n- `action.update(dt)` †: move the bodies one step; returns true while the action runs (false once it has ended)\n- `action.beat` †: the name of the beat playing now\n- `action.beats` †: [[name, seconds], ...]\n- `action.body`, `action.other` †: the bodies it moves\n- `action.done = false` †: it has ended (or was cancelled)\n- `action.duration` †: the action's length in seconds (o.speed shortens it)\n- `action.name` †: the action's name\n- `action.o` †: the options it was given\n- `action.spec` †: its E.ACTIONS entry\n- `action.start` †: where the body was when it began\n- `action.t = 0` †: seconds played\n\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n496:- `game.script(fn, o)` †: run a coroutine on game time, in the update step: game.script(function* (game) { yield .5; yield E.until(() => door.open); yield game.tween(cam, { y: 0 }, 1); yield E.all([a, b]); ... }, { keep }). Each yield waits: a number (seconds), nothing (one step), a condition (a function, or E.until(fn)), a tween or script (until it is done), a generator (run as a script of its own, and waited for), E.all([...]) or E.any([...]) (each of these). It runs at once to its first yield. Cutscenes, boss patterns, wave timelines, tutorials, attract modes. Returns the Script\n1220:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js)\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n1224:- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n1233:- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n1234:- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n1238:- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n1241:- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n1251:- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PHuNBw9p5ba56YtxhtzQnC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
