{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017wuKos1Zc1wPV62yDXCSU2","type":"tool_result","content":"1:// The BRAWLER kit's game (a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), the\n30:const SLICES = [\n135:      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n160: * SLICE 5  BRAWLER  (Final Fight, Streets of Rage 2). A city block at dusk. Every attack is a named E.MOVES move:\n161: * J jab, cross, hook, uppercut (an E.Combo; the uppercut launches), J on a foe in your face: collar grab, knee, knee, elbow;\n163: * strings. Heavy blows knock fighters down; they get up on one knee. Waves lock the screen. Crates hide food.\n381:  const GRAB = { name: 'grab', rel: true, hand: 'L', a0: .3, a1: .05, z0: -1, z1: .4, r0: 3, r1: 6, wind: .06, active: .08, recover: .3, hold: .9, lunge: .8, blade: 0, hitAt: .4 };\n385:  // what each move does when it lands: [damage, knockback, lift]. A lift takes the target off its feet: it flies, lies down,\n463:  // a fighter: stun (flinching), knocked (off its feet), down / floor (lying, time left), rise (getting up), act (its move), grip (friction)\n474:    // the hero's move set (E.MOVES, some tuned): a 4-hit punch string, a clinch (grab, knees, elbow), a kick string, a flying kick, a sweep\n524:    knock(t, by, b);\n527:  // a blow lands on a fighter: a flinch (hurt) and a slide; with a lift, or out of life, it is knocked off its feet\n528:  function knock(c, from, [dmg, force, lift]) {\n531:    if (lift) Object.assign(c, { knocked: true, bounce: .5, friction: 1.2 });\n532:    E.knockback(from, c, force, lift);\n534:  // knocked down: fly (hurt, tipping back across the arc), hit the floor flat (a dust burst, a bounce, a smaller one), lie\n537:    if (!c.knocked) return;\n541:    else if (c.rise > 0 && (c.rise -= dt) <= 0) Object.assign(c, { knocked: false, bounce: 0, friction: c.grip, t: .8 });\n552:  // of the string connects. Out of life: knocked down, then up again (a life lost) or game over\n556:    spark(x, h.y + 1, z, b[2] > 0); knock(h, f, more ? [b[0], 8, 0] : b); h.flash = game.real + .05; h.inv = more ? 0 : .6; chainT = 0;\n565:    const air = !h.onGround, busy = !!(h.act && h.act.busy), free = h.hp > 0 && !h.knocked && h.stun <= 0 && !won && !truce;\n567:    if (!h.knocked && h.stun <= 0) { const stop = busy && !air; h.vx = approach(h.vx, stop ? 0 : md[0] * 82, 900 * dt); h.vy = approach(h.vy, stop ? 0 : md[1] * 52, 900 * dt); }\n572:      const hug = foes.some(f => !f.knocked && Math.abs(f.y - h.y) < 8 && E.inArc(h, h.facing, f, 20, .9)), key = tap('kick') ? 'kick' : 'attack';\n580:    const wide = h.act === h.moves.sweep, inReach = t => !t.knocked && Math.abs(t.y - h.y) < (wide ? 18 : 12) && E.inArc(h, h.facing, t, 32, wide ? 1.9 : 1.1);\n581:    const grab = t => { if (t.box) return; if (t.act) t.act.cancel(); Object.assign(t, { act: null, stun: .9, vx: 0, vy: 0, y: h.y, x: h.x + (t.x > h.x ? 20 : -20) }); };   // the collar grab: held close\n582:    if (h.act) h.act.hits(foes.concat(boxes), inReach, t => h.act.state.spec.name === 'grab' ? grab(t) : strike(t, h.act.state, h));   // moves connect late in the strike (hitAt)\n595:      const sz = c.rig.o.size, st = c.act && c.act.state, ok = !c.knocked && c.stun <= 0, low = st && st.spec.name === 'sweep' && !(st.phase === 'recover' && st.u > .6);\n596:      const fly = c.knocked && !c.down && !(c.rise > 0);\n599:      c.rig.update(dt, Object.assign({ x: c.x, y: c.y, z: c.z, vx: c.vx / sz, vy: c.vy / sz, facing: pose(c.facing), air: !c.onGround && !c.knocked, stance: ok ? 'guard' : null,\n623:        f.act.hits(heroes, t => t.inv <= 0 && !t.knocked && Math.abs(t.y - f.y) < 12 && E.inArc(f, f.facing, t, 16 + 6 * sz, 1), t => hurtHero(f, f.act.state, t));\nchromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\n424:- `r.marker(x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: an objective marker over a world point: a bobbing diamond (and its label) while it is on screen, an arrow at the screen's edge pointing to it while it is off (offscreen: false hides it then). o: { label, color: '#ffd040', offscreen: 'arrow' }\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest,\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"5f74995c-a47e-405a-a7ae-0cd046505cc2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:59:51.900Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:// The BRAWLER kit's game (a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage), readable: the starter's shell (src/starter/00-shell.js), the\n30:const SLICES = [\n135:      E.font.text(g, SLICES[titleMenu.i].about, r.W / 2, r.H - 14, '#ffe7a8', { align: 'center', shadow: '#000', outline: false });\n160: * SLICE 5  BRAWLER  (Final Fight, Streets of Rage 2). A city block at dusk. Every attack is a named E.MOVES move:\n161: * J jab, cross, hook, uppercut (an E.Combo; the uppercut launches), J on a foe in your face: collar grab, knee, knee, elbow;\n163: * strings. Heavy blows knock fighters down; they get up on one knee. 