{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AeZD1F7s9Ro8Yn6bFDswTE","type":"tool_result","content":"426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"ddbb944e-60c5-40a5-93fb-3acb8c93653c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:12:22.391Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or a body's size round its point). [] for none\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AeZD1F7s9Ro8Yn6bFDswTE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
