{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2E2bDwNiwvCu9LSMEi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EY6RuNXdiaGmvA7aDWMYwn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":597,"limit":50},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2549,"cache_read_input_tokens":417141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2549},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"34c24cea-910d-44e0-ac15-16075ca8d316","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:29:46.079Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2E2L6X1yQg9UkuuXFm","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EY6RuNXdiaGmvA7aDWMYwn":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":597,"limit":50}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EY6RuNXdiaGmvA7aDWMYwn","type":"tool_result","content":"597\t### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n598\t\n599\t- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n600\t  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n601\t  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n602\t- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.35 + 0.15 ×\n603\t  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players; each human\n604\t  press of ✕ adds `mashWeight` (0.04); CPU sides press at `cpuMash` per second (± 20%).\n605\t- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n606\t  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n607\t  foul if seen.\n608\t- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n609\t  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n610\t- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n611\t  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n612\t- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n613\t  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n614\t  draws the line.\n615\t\n616\t### 7.9 Scrum\n617\t\n618\t- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n619\t  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n620\t- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n621\t  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n622\t- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n623\t  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n624\t  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n625\t- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n626\t  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n627\t  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n628\t- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n629\t  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n630\t  (5 points; the conversion from in front of the posts' line at the scrum's y).\n631\t\n632\t### 7.10 Lineout\n633\t\n634\t- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n635\t  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n636\t- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n637\t  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n638\t  couch play).\n639\t- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n640\t  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n641\t- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n642\t  chose the same pod, their jumper contests: the defence wins if its jump press (✕ when the ball arrives, ±0.15 s) is\n643\t  better than the throw's quality plus the jumper's HND; else the throwers win. The winner taps it down to his\n644\t  scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three times running); CPU guesses\n645\t  right with its difficulty's read chance.\n646\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"75e6a82e-94e2-4b93-a9e9-3ab9560af1b3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:29:46.087Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 7.8 The breakdown: ruck, jackal, \"use it\"\n\n- After a successful tackle the carrier goes to ground and places the ball behind him (toward his team). The ruck\n  mark is the ball. The nearest two attackers and one or two defenders within 80 u commit (CPU); a human joins by\n  running into the 16 u ruck zone (his player then locks into the ruck pose).\n- **The contest** (`ruckTime`, 1.6 s): a tug-of-war bar from -1 (defence) to +1 (attack), starting at +0.35 + 0.15 ×\n  (attackers - defenders committed). Each second each side adds 0.02 × the POW of its committed players; each human\n  press of ✕ adds `mashWeight` (0.04); CPU sides press at `cpuMash` per second (± 20%).\n- **Jackal:** the first defender to reach the ball, if he arrives before any attacker and within 0.35 s of the tackle,\n  may press □ to jackal: the bar swings -0.5 at once (\"JACKAL!\"). Pressing □ while not first is **hands in the ruck**: a\n  foul if seen.\n- **Result:** bar ≥ 0: the attacking scrum-half (or the nearest attacker) has the ball at the base; < 0: turnover, the\n  defence picks it up and play goes on the other way. The attack's human seat switches to the receiver.\n- **\"USE IT!\":** once the ball is at the base, the referee wants it out within 3 s (a countdown ring around the ball);\n  if not, a scrum to the other team.\n- **Offside line:** while a ruck is on, each team's offside line is its hindmost committed player's feet; a non-ruck\n  player in front of his line who moves toward the ball when it comes out is offside (§7.13). The AI retreats; the HUD\n  draws the line.\n\n### 7.9 Scrum\n\n- Awarded for a knock-on, a forward pass, an unplayable ruck (\"use it\"), not straight, the 5 m restarts. The mark: at\n  least 51 u from touch and from the try lines. The non-offending team feeds.\n- **Setup** (1.5 s): the three forwards each side bind (props either side of the hooker), scrum-halves at the side,\n  backs line up 51 u behind the last feet.\n- **Engage:** the referee calls **CROUCH** (0.6 s), **BIND** (0.6 s), **SET!** A ring closes on SET: ✕ within ±0.12 s\n  = PERFECT (+0.25 on the push bar), ±0.25 s = GOOD (+0.1), later = nothing. Pressing before SET appears = **early\n  engagement**: a free kick to the other team.\n- **Push** (2.0 s): alternate L1 / R1 (Q / E): each alternating press adds `scrumPushWeight` (0.05); repeating a button\n  counts half. The feeding team starts +0.15; each side adds 0.01 per second per POW point of its three forwards. CPU\n  presses at its difficulty's rate.\n- **Result:** the side with the bar on its side wins the ball at the scrum-half. Bar beyond 0.85: the losing scrum\n  collapses (SCRUM PENALTY to the winners); if that winner is attacking within 50 u of the try line: **PUSHOVER TRY!**\n  (5 points; the conversion from in front of the posts' line at the scrum's y).\n\n### 7.10 Lineout\n\n- After touch. The line: three pods (FRONT, MIDDLE, BACK) 16 u apart from 51 u in from touch; each team's three\n  forwards stand in their line, the throwing team's hooker throws.\n- **Call** (up to 2.5 s): each side picks a pod: L1/R1 or up/down (or click a pod). The throwing team's call is shown\n  only to its own players when the opponent is human on another device; on a shared screen, both are shown (honest\n  couch play).\n- **Throw:** ✕ stops a moving needle; in the green band = a good throw, in the edges = a wobbly one, outside = **NOT\n  STRAIGHT** (scrum to the other team).\n- **Jump:** the throwing team's jumper is lifted at its pod (lifters hoist him to z 60: \"INTO ORBIT!\"). If the defenders\n  chose the same pod, their jumper contests: the defence wins if its jump press (✕ when the ball arrives, ±0.15 s) is\n  better than the throw's quality plus the jumper's HND; else the throwers win. The winner taps it down to his\n  scrum-half. CPU calls by weights (front .4, middle .35, back .25, never the same three times running); CPU guesses\n  right with its difficulty's read chance.\n","numLines":50,"startLine":597,"totalLines":1641}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EY6RuNXdiaGmvA7aDWMYwn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
