{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018cfxAmnHGPKJZ4y56VCvGw","type":"tool_result","content":"| **Muddington Park** (Mudlarks' home; the training ground too, by day without rain) | overcast day; a small wooden stand (`face: 'plank'`) and grass banks; the Muddy Duck pub behind the east in-goal | low hills, a church spire, drizzle | THE MUDDY DUCK · PIES & PINTS, BIG DAVE'S BUSES, CHANNEL THUD | \"Mud and Glory\" |\n| **Port Grumble Docks** | dusk, orange sky; a concrete stand; shipping containers stacked behind one end | cranes, a lighthouse, gulls wheeling | SEAGULL-PROOF CHIPS, KRAKEN INSURANCE, GRUMBLE'S GRAVY | \"Grumble Shanty\" |\n| **The Furnace** | night, floodlights (4 towers); black steel stands (`face: 'stone'` dark); glowing grates | chimneys belching sparks, a red glow | FORGEWORKS STEEL, TURBO TONIC, MEGA MEAT PIES | \"Forge Floor\" |\n| **The Megadome** | night storm; a huge gold and purple bowl, a jumbotron on the far stand, lasers on tries | city towers, a GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS sign | GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS, CHANNEL THUD, TURBO TONIC | \"Megadome Mayhem\" |\n\nLighting: day `lights.enabled = false`; dusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool\nunder each tower, `lights.add` every draw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames. Crowd: stand tiles hold two figures\neach (as the sports kit) in the two teams' colours (home 70%), bobbing; they jump on scores and boo cards; a Mexican wave\nrolls round when play is stopped longer than 8 s. Floodlight towers: tall lamp props or custom shapes on the stand\ncorners.\n\n### 9.3 The Mega Cup: story beats and script\n----\n\n## 13. Attract mode\n\n- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it (`E.Arcade` with `idle: 10` drives\n  the cycle; its demo phase goes to the match scene with `{ attract: true }`, its scores phase shows the records).\n- It is a CPU vs CPU match (teams and venue rotate through all four venues across loops) with cheats on: no clock,\n  hype on demand, events forced. A **director** (`game.script`) walks a showcase list, using the same `game.debug.force`\n  calls as the dev panel, each step when the previous one finished (or 12 s passed):\n  1. walk-out and kick-off; 2. a run with a sidestep and a fend; 3. a pass chain along the line with a dummy; 4. a\n  MONSTER HIT and its replay; 5. a ruck with a jackal; 6. a knock-on and a scrum; 7. a kick to touch and a lineout; 8. a\n  power-up thrown on and taken; 9. the venue's hazard; 10. THUNDER RUN to a try, the celebration, the replay; 11. the\n  conversion in the kicker's camera; 12. a cheap shot behind the ref's back, then one he sees: a yellow card and the sin\n  bin; 13. a player ON FIRE scoring; 14. a drop goal. Then the logo and the records for 8 s, then the title.\n- Overlays: \"DEMO\" top centre, a blinking \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (or \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" on touch-only), the\n  logo small in a corner; the HUD and commentary as in a real match.\n- Any input exits at once: a key, a mouse button or movement over 8 px, a pad button or a stick past 0.5, a tap. The\n  exiting input is consumed (`consumeAll`) so it does not also pick a menu item. It returns to the title.\n- Attract never writes saves or records and never runs in an AI Hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Dev mode\n\n### 14.1 The panel\n\n- Pause menu → **DEV MODE** turns dev mode on for the visit and opens the panel over the match (from the title: the\n  menu's ABOUT page has DEV MODE too, which starts an Exhibition with the panel open). Keyboard: ` toggles it once on.\n- A canvas panel, 10-foot sized (scale 1 rows, eight rows visible, scrolling), docked on the right 45% of the screen.\n  Tabs: **TUNING · CHEATS · EVENTS · VIEW · JUMP** (L1/R1 or Q/E or click). D-pad or stick moves the focus; left/right\n  changes a slider (held: repeats and speeds up); ✕ toggles or fires; □ resets the focused slider; △ switches\n  **FROZEN** (the match stopped, `timeScale` 0, the default) and **LIVE** (the match runs; the panel stays and takes the\n----\n2. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`; `null` → the normal game\n   (title).\n3. Setup from `AIHub.rng('setup')` (the same on every copy, no messages needed): the home side is the Mudlarks, the away\n   side one of the four rivals, the venue one of four, the weather the venue's. Seats: even ids HOME, odd AWAY (2\n   players 1v1, 3 players 2v1, 4 players 2v2); CPU fills the rest. Halves: `min(75, (limitMs / 1000 - 40) / 2.6)` s\n   of running clock; no sudden death (a draw is a tie).\n4. Build the match (boot steps), then show **our card** (scene `card`) and call `AIHub.ready()` once, with no key press.\n   The card: the venue at dusk, both teams lined up, each human's player in front with the hub name in the seat colour\n   (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) and a READY tick from the `card` event's `ready`; \"HOW TO WIN: score more\n----\n- **Snapshot budget:** 99% of snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (tested, §19.3); if a build exceeds it, send players 0-6 and 7-13\n  in alternate snapshots.\n- **Rules in a session:** no network but the hub; no chat, emotes or custom names (names from the hub, never inserted\n  as HTML: the canvas font draws them); no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; no title, restart\n  or quit; Options is ignored while Create is held; nothing outside a session changes.\n\n---\n\n----\n\n### 19.6 The AI Hub harness\n\nServe the dev folder's `hub/` (holding the harness files and a copy of the built HTML) with `python3 -m http.server 0\n--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), check the page at `/` is ours (its title is \"Thugby Turbo\"),\nthen with Playwright open `harness.html?game=<html>&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\nthe same with `&scenario=host-leave`; and `&players=2&scenario=server`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete ===\n'true'`; pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true; print failing checks only. Stop only the server you started, by its\nPID. Then open the HTML on its own to confirm it still plays outside a session.\n\n### 19.7 Balance targets (tuned with the dev panel, measured by the `ai` suite and by hand)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"2c145105-71f5-416c-9f42-8e0c4d10a5ec","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:37.913Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"| **Muddington Park** (Mudlarks' home; the training ground too, by day without rain) | overcast day; a small wooden stand (`face: 'plank'`) and grass banks; the Muddy Duck pub behind the east in-goal | low hills, a church spire, drizzle | THE MUDDY DUCK · PIES & PINTS, BIG DAVE'S BUSES, CHANNEL THUD | \"Mud and Glory\" |\n| **Port Grumble Docks** | dusk, orange sky; a concrete stand; shipping containers stacked behind one end | cranes, a lighthouse, gulls wheeling | SEAGULL-PROOF CHIPS, KRAKEN INSURANCE, GRUMBLE'S GRAVY | \"Grumble Shanty\" |\n| **The Furnace** | night, floodlights (4 towers); black steel stands (`face: 'stone'` dark); glowing grates | chimneys belching sparks, a red glow | FORGEWORKS STEEL, TURBO TONIC, MEGA MEAT PIES | \"Forge Floor\" |\n| **The Megadome** | night storm; a huge gold and purple bowl, a jumbotron on the far stand, lasers on tries | city towers, a GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS sign | GOLDBRICK HOLDINGS, CHANNEL THUD, TURBO TONIC | \"Megadome Mayhem\" |\n\nLighting: day `lights.enabled = false`; dusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool\nunder each tower, `lights.add` every draw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames. Crowd: stand tiles hold two figures\neach (as the sports kit) in the two teams' colours (home 70%), bobbing; they jump on scores and boo cards; a Mexican wave\nrolls round when play is stopped longer than 8 s. Floodlight towers: tall lamp props or custom shapes on the stand\ncorners.\n\n### 9.3 The Mega Cup: story beats and script\n----\n\n## 13. Attract mode\n\n- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it (`E.Arcade` with `idle: 10` drives\n  the cycle; its demo phase goes to the match scene with `{ attract: true }`, its scores phase shows the records).\n- It is a CPU vs CPU match (teams and venue rotate through all four venues across loops) with cheats on: no clock,\n  hype on demand, events forced. A **director** (`game.script`) walks a showcase list, using the same `game.debug.force`\n  calls as the dev panel, each step when the previous one finished (or 12 s passed):\n  1. walk-out and kick-off; 2. a run with a sidestep and a fend; 3. a pass chain along the line with a dummy; 4. a\n  MONSTER HIT and its replay; 5. a ruck with a jackal; 6. a knock-on and a scrum; 7. a kick to touch and a lineout; 8. a\n  power-up thrown on and taken; 9. the venue's hazard; 10. THUNDER RUN to a try, the celebration, the replay; 11. the\n  conversion in the kicker's camera; 12. a cheap shot behind the ref's back, then one he sees: a yellow card and the sin\n  bin; 13. a player ON FIRE scoring; 14. a drop goal. Then the logo and the records for 8 s, then the title.\n- Overlays: \"DEMO\" top centre, a blinking \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (or \"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\" on touch-only), the\n  logo small in a corner; the HUD and commentary as in a real match.\n- Any input exits at once: a key, a mouse button or movement over 8 px, a pad button or a stick past 0.5, a tap. The\n  exiting input is consumed (`consumeAll`) so it does not also pick a menu item. It returns to the title.\n- Attract never writes saves or records and never runs in an AI Hub session.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Dev mode\n\n### 14.1 The panel\n\n- Pause menu → **DEV MODE** turns dev mode on for the visit and opens the panel over the match (from the title: the\n  menu's ABOUT page has DEV MODE too, which starts an Exhibition with the panel open). Keyboard: ` toggles it once on.\n- A canvas panel, 10-foot sized (scale 1 rows, eight rows visible, scrolling), docked on the right 45% of the screen.\n  Tabs: **TUNING · CHEATS · EVENTS · VIEW · JUMP** (L1/R1 or Q/E or click). D-pad or stick moves the focus; left/right\n  changes a slider (held: repeats and speeds up); ✕ toggles or fires; □ resets the focused slider; △ switches\n  **FROZEN** (the match stopped, `timeScale` 0, the default) and **LIVE** (the match runs; the panel stays and takes the\n----\n2. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [2, 4], card: true })`; `null` → the normal game\n   (title).\n3. Setup from `AIHub.rng('setup')` (the same on every copy, no messages needed): the home side is the Mudlarks, the away\n   side one of the four rivals, the venue one of four, the weather the venue's. Seats: even ids HOME, odd AWAY (2\n   players 1v1, 3 players 2v1, 4 players 2v2); CPU fills the rest. Halves: `min(75, (limitMs / 1000 - 40) / 2.6)` s\n   of running clock; no sudden death (a draw is a tie).\n4. Build the match (boot steps), then show **our card** (scene `card`) and call `AIHub.ready()` once, with no key press.\n   The card: the venue at dusk, both teams lined up, each human's player in front with the hub name in the seat colour\n   (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`) and a READY tick from the `card` event's `ready`; \"HOW TO WIN: score more\n----\n- **Snapshot budget:** 99% of snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes (tested, §19.3); if a build exceeds it, send players 0-6 and 7-13\n  in alternate snapshots.\n- **Rules in a session:** no network but the hub; no chat, emotes or custom names (names from the hub, never inserted\n  as HTML: the canvas font draws them); no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation; no title, restart\n  or quit; Options is ignored while Create is held; nothing outside a session changes.\n\n---\n\n----\n\n### 19.6 The AI Hub harness\n\nServe the dev folder's `hub/` (holding the harness files and a copy of the built HTML) with `python3 -m http.server 0\n--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), check the page at `/` is ours (its title is \"Thugby Turbo\"),\nthen with Playwright open `harness.html?game=<html>&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\nthe same with `&scenario=host-leave`; and `&players=2&scenario=server`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete ===\n'true'`; pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true; print failing checks only. Stop only the server you started, by its\nPID. Then open the HTML on its own to confirm it still plays outside a session.\n\n### 19.7 Balance targets (tuned with the dev panel, measured by the `ai` suite and by hand)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018cfxAmnHGPKJZ4y56VCvGw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2J7y2pXvpaZP485oET","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SQxyzXQg1ecje61Hwa6Sag","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"Lighting: day `lights.enabled = false`; dusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool\\nunder each tower, `lights.add` every draw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames.\",\n \"Lighting (every scene is lit, as the look target asks): day `lights.enabled = true` with ambient 0.95 and a warm tint;\\ndusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool under each tower, `lights.add` every\\ndraw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames.\"),\n(\"| Skylines per venue | painted in `r.overlay`-free world space behind the far stand: silhouettes anchored to the stand's projected top edge, drawn after `r.sky` and before the map |\",\n \"| Skylines per venue | the TileMap has `outside: false`; each draw paints `r.sky([...])`, then the venue's silhouettes (hills, cranes, chimneys, towers) anchored to the far stand's projected top edge (`r.w` of its back corners), then the map, so the stand meets the skyline whatever the camera does |\"),\n(\"- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it (`E.Arcade` with `idle: 10` drives\\n  the cycle; its demo phase goes to the match scene with `{ attract: true }`, its scores phase shows the records).\",\n \"- On `title` and `menu` (and `records`, `about`): 10 s without any input starts it. One `new E.Arcade(game, { id:\\n  'thugby', idle: 10, demo: 300, scores: 8, hud: false })`; those scenes call `arcade.attract(dt)` each step; when\\n  `arcade.phase` turns `'demo'` they `game.go('match', { attract: true })`; the director calls `arcade.endDemo()` and\\n  goes back to the title at its end (the `'scores'` phase then shows the records with `arcade.drawTable`); an exit by\\n  input calls `arcade.wake()`. Our own idle check (below) also counts mouse movement and sticks.\"),\n(\"- Pause menu → **DEV MODE** turns dev mode on for the visit and opens the panel over the match (from the title: the\\n  menu's ABOUT page has DEV MODE too, which starts an Exhibition with the panel open). Keyboard: ` toggles it once on.\",\n \"- Pause menu → **DEV MODE** (in every pausable scene: matches and drills) turns dev mode on for the visit and opens\\n  the panel over the play. After that, ` (backquote) toggles it from the keyboard. Its JUMP tab reaches every other\\n  part of the game.\"),\n(\"CPU fills the rest. Halves: `min(75, (limitMs / 1000 - 40) / 2.6)` s\\n   of running clock; no sudden death (a draw is a tie).\",\n \"CPU fills the rest. Halves: `min(75, (limitMs / 1000 - 40) / 2.6)` s\\n   of running clock (75 when `limitMs` is 0); no sudden death (a draw is a tie).\"),\n(\"no chat, emotes or custom names (names from the hub, never inserted\\n  as HTML: the canvas font draws them);\",\n \"no chat, emotes or custom names (names from the hub, never inserted\\n  as HTML: the pixel font draws them, accents stripped with `normalize('NFD')` and any other character it lacks shown\\n  as a dot);\"),\n(\"or quit; Options is ignored while Create is held; nothing outside a session changes.\",\n \"or quit; Options is ignored while Create is held; no hit-stop (`game.freeze` would stall the host's sends: hits use\\n  `particles.impact`, sparks, shake and a sound instead, and each copy may hold its drawn frame for 60 ms); nothing\\n  outside a session changes.\"),\n(\"with `python3 -m http.server 0\\n--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), check the page at `/` is ours (its title is \\\"Thugby Turbo\\\"),\\nthen\",\n \"with `python3 -m http.server 0\\n--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), fetch the copied HTML from that port and check its `<title>`\\nis \\\"Thugby Turbo\\\" (another agent's server may hold a port: never trust a page you have not checked), then\"),\n(\"| 1 | \\\"BIG UNIT\\\" Brannigan (captain, the boss) | Prop | bulky **2.0** | bald, a gold headband | 6 12 6 3 10 |\",\n \"| 1 | \\\"BIG UNIT\\\" Brannigan (captain, the boss) | Prop | bulky **2.0** | bald, a gold headband | 6 12 6 3 10 (POW beyond the scale on purpose) |\"),\n]\nfor a, b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF","description":"Apply a batch of precise text fixes to PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2837,"cache_read_input_tokens":427847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2837},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"7fcd9402-63f6-4511-a72f-d2cb03c0bced","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:30:54.859Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2J7fBxKc9xJ2mKA7eD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01SQxyzXQg1ecje61Hwa6Sag":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"Lighting: day `lights.enabled = false`; dusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool\\nunder each tower, `lights.add` every draw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames.\",\n \"Lighting (every scene is lit, as the look target asks): day `lights.enabled = true` with ambient 0.95 and a warm tint;\\ndusk ambient 0.65 with floodlights; night 0.45 with floodlights (a light pool under each tower, `lights.add` every\\ndraw) and emissive fire, sparks and flames.\"),\n(\"| Skylines per venue | painted in `r.overlay`-free w