{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MFapsN2zQnsy6Ni6A28cim","type":"tool_result","content":"### 6.3 Presets and two players on one keyboard\n\nOne preset object `KEYS` (actions `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` plus the engine's `up down left right start pause\nconfirm cancel`), codes from the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5`\nR1, `Pad6` L2 unused, `Pad7` R2, `Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\n\n| Half | Move | Turbo | ✕ | □ | ○ | △ | L1 | R1 | Start / pause |\ncones, floodlight towers, sponsor boards, the sin bin, cameramen on the touchline as small Humanoids with a box camera);\neffects on every hit; `E.font.title` logos with 3-4 colour gradients and depth; light in every night scene; portraits in\nevery dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\nnot with NES ones.\n\n### 19.1 One command\n\n`node test/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) rebuilds, runs every headless suite, and prints **only failures** (`FAIL\nsuite › case: message`) and **one line**: `N passed, M failed (S suites, T s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--only\n<suite>` reruns one suite (rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers). `--browser` adds the Playwright\nchecks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way).\n\n### 19.2 The harness","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"bfbfc8d3-a2a3-4931-b09c-5434bbeb15c8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:31:07.420Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 6.3 Presets and two players on one keyboard\n\nOne preset object `KEYS` (actions `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` plus the engine's `up down left right start pause\nconfirm cancel`), codes from the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5`\nR1, `Pad6` L2 unused, `Pad7` R2, `Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\n\n| Half | Move | Turbo | ✕ | □ | ○ | △ | L1 | R1 | Start / pause |\ncones, floodlight towers, sponsor boards, the sin bin, cameramen on the touchline as small Humanoids with a box camera);\neffects on every hit; `E.font.title` logos with 3-4 colour gradients and depth; light in every night scene; portraits in\nevery dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\nnot with NES ones.\n\n### 19.1 One command\n\n`node test/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) rebuilds, runs every headless suite, and prints **only failures** (`FAIL\nsuite › case: message`) and **one line**: `N passed, M failed (S suites, T s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--only\n<suite>` reruns one suite (rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers). `--browser` adds the Playwright\nchecks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way).\n\n### 19.2 The harness","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01MFapsN2zQnsy6Ni6A28cim","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2LJ6o82r1DzfSqz54k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012D8NxHo3QjbHNLQ8dPfPrc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"One preset object `KEYS` (actions `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` plus the engine's `up down left right start pause\\nconfirm cancel`), codes from the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5`\\nR1, `Pad6` L2 unused, `Pad7` R2, `Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\",\n \"One preset object `KEYS`, built as the sports kit builds its own: start from `E.Input.DEFAULT` (its moves and its menu\\nactions `start pause confirm cancel`), delete `attack dash skill jump`, add `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` with the\\ncodes in the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5` R1, `Pad7` R2,\\n`Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3; L2 is left free). Use it on every play scene (`input: KEYS`). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\"),\n(\"every dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\\nnot with NES ones.\",\n \"every dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\\nnot with NES ones. Performance is out of scope (TASK.md): favour detail (full crowds, lights, particles, shadows) over\\nframe rate.\"),\n(\"checks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way).\",\n \"checks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way). Tests are scripts that play the game and check its\\nstate through `game.advance` and `game.debug`; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or\\nworkflows to debate, review, judge or audit (TASK.md).\"),\n(\"| `uiScale` | Display | TV text size | Large · Normal (Large raises HUD prompts to scale 2 and the shell CSS above) |\",\n \"| `uiScale` | Display | TV text size | Large · Normal (Large raises HUD prompts to scale 2 and the shell CSS above) |\\n| `camera` | Display | Camera | Broadcast · High · Overhead (the views of §5.3; R3 and V cycle them in play) |\"),\n(\"a placeholder-free stub (a title scene with the logo) |\",\n \"a placeholder-free stub (a title scene with the logo). Practical notes: `/tmp` on this machine was full during\\nplanning, so keep scratch files in the dev folder; take the engine's `dist/handoff` with `git clone --depth 1` of\\nmy-3d2dge (about 150 MB) and the hub files with `curl` (the ai-hub repository is over 5 GB: do not clone it) |\"),\n]\nfor a, b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF","description":"Add preset, performance, testing-rule, camera and setup notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":747,"cache_read_input_tokens":433450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":747},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"e8476d4f-93fb-4486-90fe-dd05395e5d79","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:31:19.950Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2LHqAh3Wvpo48SwqVg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012D8NxHo3QjbHNLQ8dPfPrc":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nreps = [\n(\"One preset object `KEYS` (actions `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` plus the engine's `up down left right start pause\\nconfirm cancel`), codes from the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5`\\nR1, `Pad6` L2 unused, `Pad7` R2, `Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\",\n \"One preset object `KEYS`, built as the sports kit builds its own: start from `E.Input.DEFAULT` (its moves and its menu\\nactions `start pause confirm cancel`), delete `attack dash skill jump`, add `x, sq, ci, tri, l1, r1, turbo` with the\\ncodes in the tables above (pad codes: `Pad0` ✕, `Pad1` ○, `Pad2` □, `Pad3` △, `Pad4` L1, `Pad5` R1, `Pad7` R2,\\n`Pad9` Options, `Pad11` R3; L2 is left free). Use it on every play scene (`input: KEYS`). `KEYS.halves` (patch 2):\"),\n(\"every dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\\nnot with NES ones.\",\n \"every dialog. Act on every look note `tools/check.mjs` prints. Compare screenshots with the best PS1-era sports games,\\nnot with NES ones. Performance is out of scope (TASK.md): favour detail (full crowds, lights, particles, shadows) over\\nframe rate.\"),\n(\"checks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way).\",\n \"checks, `--hub` the AI Hub harness runs (both print the same way). Tests are scripts that play the game and check its\\nstate through `game.advance` and `game.debug`; screenshots only for what a script cannot check; no subagents or\\nworkflows to debate, review, judge or audit (TASK.md).\"),\n(\"| `uiScale` | Display | TV text size | Large · Normal (Large raises HUD prompts to scale 2 and the shell CSS above) |\",\n \"| `uiScale` | Display | TV text size | Large · Normal (Large raises HUD prompts to scale 2 and the shell CSS above) |\\n| `camera` | Display | Camera | Broadcast · High · Overhead (the views of §5.3; R3 and V cycle them in play) |\"),\n(\"a placeholder-free stub (a title scene with the logo) |\",\n \"a placeholder-free stub (a title scene with the logo). Practical notes: `/tmp` on this machine was full during\\nplanning, so keep scratch files in the dev folder; take the engine's `dist/handoff` with `git clone --depth 1` of\\nmy-3d2dge (about 150 MB) and the hub files with `curl` (the ai-hub repository is over 5 GB: do not clone it) |\"),\n]\nfor a, b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF","description":"Add preset, performance, testing-rule, camera and setup notes"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_012D8NxHo3QjbHNLQ8dPfPrc":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work"}}}
