{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2QThMj8CCtJoVirETm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jp19HLPCKEMhV4XPpyqLf8","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":440,"limit":80},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1293,"cache_read_input_tokens":438987,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1293},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"6b55fa7d-b5cd-41b7-a228-c0b89fb0f234","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:09.214Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2QTRyy5MpyHee3QRcc","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Jp19HLPCKEMhV4XPpyqLf8":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":440,"limit":80}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jp19HLPCKEMhV4XPpyqLf8","type":"tool_result","content":"440\t  scale 1 in the HUD (scale 2 on big prompts).\n441\t\n442\t### 6.5 Assists\n443\t\n444\tSettings, Game: **Auto-switch** (Assisted: to the defender nearest the ball each time the ball is passed or kicked, and\n445\ton ✕ when no one is in range; Full: always the best defender; Manual: only by buttons and mouse). **Pass assist** (On:\n446\ta pass button with no legal receiver on that side throws to the nearest legal one on the other side; Off: it is a\n447\tdummy, §7.4). **Hold or toggle** turbo.\n448\t\n449\t### 6.6 Touch-only devices\n450\t\n451\t- Detect: `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad\n452\t  has been seen and no key pressed. Re-check on `gamepadconnected`, `keydown` and `pointermove` with a mouse: any of\n453\t  them leaves touch-only mode at once.\n454\t- In touch-only mode: no touch buttons or stick anywhere (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, every scene `touch: []`);\n455\t  the title shows **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** (scale 2) with \"Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" and a\n456\t  big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`); the attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap during it\n457\t  goes back to the title.\n458\t\n459\t---\n460\t\n461\t## 7. Match systems (rules and numbers)\n462\t\n463\tAll numbers are `TUNE` defaults (§14.2). \"u\" = world units.\n464\t\n465\t### 7.1 Match flow and clock\n466\t\n467\tPhases (`state.phase`), each with a watchdog (any phase longer than its limit resolves itself and emits a `watchdog`\n468\tevent that tests fail on):\n469\t\n470\t```\n471\tintro → kickoff → play ⇄ (tackle → ruck → play)\n472\t                       ⇄ (knockOn | forwardPass → scrum → play)\n473\t                       ⇄ (touch → lineout → play)\n474\t                       ⇄ (foul → [advantage] → penalty → choice → setKick | tapGo | kickToTouch→lineout)\n475\t                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n476\t          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n477\t          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\n478\thooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n479\t```\n480\t\n481\t- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n482\t  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n483\t  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n484\t- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n485\t  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n486\t- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n487\t- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n488\t  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n489\t- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n490\t\n491\t### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n492\t\n493\t- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n494\t  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n495\t  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n496\t- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n497\t  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n498\t- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n499\t  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n500\t- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n501\t  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n502\t  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n503\t- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n504\t  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n505\t  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n506\t- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n507\t  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n508\t  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n509\t    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n510\t    ground.\n511\t  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n512\t    seat colour.\n513\t\n514\t### 7.3 The ball\n515\t\n516\t- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n517\t  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n518\t- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) with no walls; air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s;\n519\t  wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"cb3611a8-7547-4b89-8052-f6b0b01c8cd2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:09.220Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"  scale 1 in the HUD (scale 2 on big prompts).\n\n### 6.5 Assists\n\nSettings, Game: **Auto-switch** (Assisted: to the defender nearest the ball each time the ball is passed or kicked, and\non ✕ when no one is in range; Full: always the best defender; Manual: only by buttons and mouse). **Pass assist** (On:\na pass button with no legal receiver on that side throws to the nearest legal one on the other side; Off: it is a\ndummy, §7.4). **Hold or toggle** turbo.\n\n### 6.6 Touch-only devices\n\n- Detect: `matchMedia('(any-pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad\n  has been seen and no key pressed. Re-check on `gamepadconnected`, `keydown` and `pointermove` with a mouse: any of\n  them leaves touch-only mode at once.\n- In touch-only mode: no touch buttons or stick anywhere (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, every scene `touch: []`);\n  the title shows **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** (scale 2) with \"Connect a controller or a keyboard to play.\" and a\n  big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`); the attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap during it\n  goes back to the title.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Match systems (rules and numbers)\n\nAll numbers are `TUNE` defaults (§14.2). \"u\" = world units.\n\n### 7.1 Match flow and clock\n\nPhases (`state.phase`), each with a watchdog (any phase longer than its limit resolves itself and emits a `watchdog`\nevent that tests fail on):\n\n```\nintro → kickoff → play ⇄ (tackle → ruck → play)\n                       ⇄ (knockOn | forwardPass → scrum → play)\n                       ⇄ (touch → lineout → play)\n                       ⇄ (foul → [advantage] → penalty → choice → setKick | tapGo | kickToTouch→lineout)\n                       ⇄ (deadBall → dropOut → play)\n          → try → celebrate [→ replay] → conversion → kickoff (the scoring team kicks off)\n          → dropGoal | penaltyGoal → kickoff\nhooter → (next stoppage) → halftime → kickoff (2nd half, other team) → hooter → fulltime | suddenDeath → results\n```\n\n- Halves: `halfLength` = 120 s of **running** clock (stops at stoppages: set-piece setups, conversions, penalties,\n  celebrations, replays, cutscenes). The TV clock shows sevens time, 0:00 to 7:00 per half (`shown = run × 420 /\n  halfLength`). Settings: 2 / 3 / 4 / 5 minute halves (120 / 180 / 240 / 300 s).\n- At zero: the HOOTER sounds; the half ends at the next stoppage (ball dead, a score, a tackle completed, a set piece\n  awarded), so the last play is live. If open play runs 30 s past the hooter, the next tackle ends it.\n- Kick-offs: the first half by the home team; the second by the away team; after any score, by the team that scored.\n- Level at full time in the cup or with \"Sudden death\" on: SUDDEN DEATH extra time, the first score of any kind wins\n  (\"GOLDEN POINT\"); if 120 s pass with no score in Exhibition, it's a draw; in the cup it goes on.\n- Halftime: a 6-8 s dressing-room overlay (the coach's line in the cup, the stats in Exhibition); ends on ✕.\n\n### 7.2 Players, movement, turbo and control\n\n- **Roles** (sevens): PROP (loosehead), HOOKER, PROP (tighthead): the forwards; SCRUM-HALF, FLY-HALF, CENTRE, WING: the\n  backs. The scrum-half takes the ball from rucks and scrums; the fly-half takes kick-offs and set kicks; the hooker\n  throws lineouts; forwards form scrums and lineouts.\n- **Stats** 1-10: SPD, POW, HND (hands), KCK, TKL. Derived: top speed `runSpeed × (0.8 + 0.04 × SPD)`; acceleration\n  `accel × (1.15 - 0.03 × POW)`; turning at 10 rad/s (8 with the ball).\n- **Movement:** an `E.Body` (`r` 5, `friction` 0, `gravity` 700) per player; velocity approaches `intent.move × speed`\n  at the acceleration; carrying the ball costs 4% speed; mud costs 20% (§7.18).\n- **Turbo:** held, it multiplies speed by `turboMult` (1.45) and drains a 3.0 s tank; it refills at 0.3 tank per second\n  after 0.6 s of not using it. Turbo also adds 10% to tackle and fend strength and, with the ball, 5% to the chance a\n  tackle breaks. Empty: it sputters (no effect, a puff sound).\n- **States** (`st`): `idle, run, carry, pass, kick, sidestep, spin, fend, charge, tackling, diving, tackled, ground,\n  getUp, stunned, ruck, scrum, lineout, lift, celebrate, binned, sentOff, walkout`. Each has its own timer `stT`. Only\n  `idle/run/carry/charge` accept movement intents.\n- **Control and switching:** each human seat drives one player of its team.\n  - The team gains the ball: the seat takes the carrier (if two humans share a team, the one whose player is nearer).\n  - Defending: Assisted auto-switch (§6.5); L1/R1 move control to the next teammate up/down the screen; ○ to the one\n    nearest the ball; a mouse click on a teammate. Never onto a player held by another seat, in the sin bin, or on the\n    ground.\n  - Controlled players show a ring under their feet and a chevron with the seat label (P1-P4, or the hub name) in the\n    seat colour.\n\n### 7.3 The ball\n\n- States: `held` (carried; drawn at the carry hand), `pass` and `kick` (in flight), `loose` (rolling or bouncing),\n  `dead` (stoppage), `placed` (in a ruck, on the tee, at the scrum feed).\n- Physics: an `E.Body` (`r` 3, `gravity` 600, `bounce` 0.45) with no walls; air drag 0.3/s; rolling friction 1.4/s;\n  wind (§7.18) pushes it while airborne.","numLines":80,"startLine":440,"totalLines":1673}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jp19HLPCKEMhV4XPpyqLf8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
