{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2RXkiBznURDBps6ZEk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AvDcpt1KenY4UYagYHiKFc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1600,"limit":76},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3991,"cache_read_input_tokens":442990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3991},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"f8eb9810-afa6-4798-939c-aee4f85e747b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:24.789Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2RXVLU8msLe7NhhTv6","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01AvDcpt1KenY4UYagYHiKFc":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","offset":1600,"limit":76}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AvDcpt1KenY4UYagYHiKFc","type":"tool_result","content":"1600\tCPU brain through the intent interface, like the sports kit's `bot()`; halves 30 s) until won (retry with CONTINUE if\n1601\tlost; the test fails after three losses) → results → cup hub (autosave checked) → quarter-final, semi-final and grand\n1602\tfinal (halves 30 s; god mode allowed for the final only, so the boss's gang-tackle rule is still exercised by the CPU)\n1603\t→ victory → third half → credits → title. It asserts the scene order, the saves, the unlocks, and no errors or\n1604\twatchdogs anywhere.\n1605\t\n1606\t### 19.5 In a browser (what scripts cannot check)\n1607\t\n1608\t- `node tools/check.mjs <final html>` (and `#scene` deep links: `#match`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#attract`): no errors,\n1609\t  look notes acted on; `--size 1920x1080` and `--size 390x844@3` (touch-only screen).\n1610\t- Screenshots to look at (once per milestone that changes them): each venue in each view; kick-off, ruck, scrum,\n1611\t  lineout, set kick, penalty choice; a monster hit; a replay; the HUD with 1 and 4 seats; each menu screen; the dev\n1612\t  panel; the hub card; results; credits.\n1613\t- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) of every move in §11.2.\n1614\t- A pad by hand if one is available (else `input.press('Pad0')` scripted in Playwright).\n1615\t\n1616\t### 19.6 The AI Hub harness\n1617\t\n1618\tServe the dev folder's `hub/` (holding the harness files and a copy of the built HTML) with `python3 -m http.server 0\n1619\t--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), fetch the copied HTML from that port and check its `<title>`\n1620\tis \"Thugby Turbo\" (another agent's server may hold a port: never trust a page you have not checked), then with Playwright open `harness.html?game=<html>&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\n1621\tthe same with `&scenario=host-leave`; and `&players=2&scenario=server`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete ===\n1622\t'true'`; pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true; print failing checks only. Stop only the server you started, by its\n1623\tPID. Then open the HTML on its own to confirm it still plays outside a session.\n1624\t\n1625\t### 19.7 Balance targets (tuned with the dev panel, measured by the `ai` suite and by hand)\n1626\t\n1627\tA Pro v Pro CPU match: 4-9 tries, 60% of conversions, 1-3 monster hits, 2-4 scrums, 2-4 lineouts, a card every two or\n1628\tthree matches, a power-up taken every 40 s. A new human on Pro wins round one about four times in five and loses the\n1629\tfinal at the first try about half the time. Turbo runs out in about one long break. A big hit should feel like an event,\n1630\tnot every tackle.\n1631\t\n1632\t---\n1633\t\n1634\t## 20. About & Credits screen and the exit interview\n1635\t\n1636\t- **About & Credits** (`about` scene, five pages at scale 1-2, L1/R1 or left/right, ✕ closes):\n1637\t  1. THUGBY TURBO: made with the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (`E.versionLabel()`), the AI Hub session client 1.4.0; by\n1638\t     the model that built it; the title's RNG pick; \"an original game inspired by rugby; every team, person and place\n1639\t     is made up\".\n1640\t  2. SOURCE INFORMATION: Date 2026-11-03 17:48:28 · Source: rugby (over-the-top arcade style) · Plan: PLAN.md · Genre\n1641\t     and perspective · Tech · Art direction · Animation · Audio · Online · Testing · Research · Environment · Model ·\n1642\t     Usage (estimates only if available; \"unknown\" otherwise).\n1643\t  3. TESTING FEEDBACK (the four answers). 4. ENGINE FEEDBACK (the six answers, including the patches and why). 5. PROMPT\n1644\t     FEEDBACK (the four answers).\n1645\t  The builder writes these from the real build at the end (M9); \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed. The\n1646\t  same text goes in the final chat reply.\n1647\t- **`exit-interview.json`** in this folder, beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape; suggested `aiHub` values:\n1648\t  name \"THUGBY TURBO\", tagline \"Big hits, bigger hair, seven a side\", description \"Over-the-top arcade rugby sevens:\n1649\t  turbo runs, monster hits, a referee who only sees half of it, and a pub team's run at the Mega Cup.\", type \"Game\",\n1650\t  genre \"Sports\", source \"Rugby\", series \"\", players \"1–4\", controls \"Stick or WASD run, L1/R1 or Q/E pass, ✕ or Space\n1651\t  tackle and sidestep, ○ or C kick, R2 or Shift turbo, △ or R super\", tags `[\"sports\", \"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"3d\",\n1652\t  \"versus\", \"co-op\"]`. Check it parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n1653\t\n1654\t---\n1655\t\n1656\t## 21. Definition of done\n1657\t\n1658\t- [ ] `ThugbyTurbo-Rugby-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174828.html` in this folder plays from `file://` with no errors;\n1659\t      the dev subfolder holds the sources, tests and tools.\n1660\t- [ ] Every system in §7 works in play and is shown by the cup, the drills or the attract mode; nothing is stubbed; no\n1661\t      TODO or placeholder text anywhere (grep the sources for TODO, FIXME, TBD, lorem, placeholder).\n1662\t- [ ] Mega Cup (prologue, training, four matches, victory, third half, credits), Exhibition (any teams, venues,\n1663\t      weather, 1-4 players), Training Ground, Records, Settings, About & Credits all reachable and complete.\n1664\t- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox in Settings; keyboard and mouse native; prompts\n1665\t      follow the last device; touch-only screen with Settings; attract mode after 10 s, any input exits.\n1666\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders for §14.2, reset to defaults, cheats, events, overlays, jumps.\n1667\t- [ ] All audio in code; babble voices for every speaker; music per scene with layers.\n1668\t- [ ] Local multiplayer 1-4; AI Hub shared-world passes the harness in all four configurations; outside a session the\n1669\t      game is unaffected.\n1670\t- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` passes, including the scripted playthrough; browser checks and screenshots reviewed.\n1671\t- [ ] Engine patches listed in `engine/PATCHES.md` and in Engine Feedback.\n1672\t- [ ] About & Credits pages and the chat reply carry Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback;\n1673\t      `exit-interview.json` parses.\n1674\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"330219a3-1af8-424b-aea5-2830d09af9ad","uuid":"3c114fb7-fa93-4d75-8654-6a7d6d2ba557","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:24.795Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174828__xe9c1ea/work/PLAN.md","content":"CPU brain through the intent interface, like the sports kit's `bot()`; halves 30 s) until won (retry with CONTINUE if\nlost; the test fails after three losses) → results → cup hub (autosave checked) → quarter-final, semi-final and grand\nfinal (halves 30 s; god mode allowed for the final only, so the boss's gang-tackle rule is still exercised by the CPU)\n→ victory → third half → credits → title. It asserts the scene order, the saves, the unlocks, and no errors or\nwatchdogs anywhere.\n\n### 19.5 In a browser (what scripts cannot check)\n\n- `node tools/check.mjs <final html>` (and `#scene` deep links: `#match`, `#cup`, `#training`, `#attract`): no errors,\n  look notes acted on; `--size 1920x1080` and `--size 390x844@3` (touch-only screen).\n- Screenshots to look at (once per milestone that changes them): each venue in each view; kick-off, ruck, scrum,\n  lineout, set kick, penalty choice; a monster hit; a replay; the HUD with 1 and 4 seats; each menu screen; the dev\n  panel; the hub card; results; credits.\n- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) of every move in §11.2.\n- A pad by hand if one is available (else `input.press('Pad0')` scripted in Playwright).\n\n### 19.6 The AI Hub harness\n\nServe the dev folder's `hub/` (holding the harness files and a copy of the built HTML) with `python3 -m http.server 0\n--bind 127.0.0.1` (note the port it prints and its PID), fetch the copied HTML from that port and check its `<title>`\nis \"Thugby Turbo\" (another agent's server may hold a port: never trust a page you have not checked), then with Playwright open `harness.html?game=<html>&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`;\nthe same with `&scenario=host-leave`; and `&players=2&scenario=server`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete ===\n'true'`; pass when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true; print failing checks only. Stop only the server you started, by its\nPID. Then open the HTML on its own to confirm it still plays outside a session.\n\n### 19.7 Balance targets (tuned with the dev panel, measured by the `ai` suite and by hand)\n\nA Pro v Pro CPU match: 4-9 tries, 60% of conversions, 1-3 monster hits, 2-4 scrums, 2-4 lineouts, a card every two or\nthree matches, a power-up taken every 40 s. A new human on Pro wins round one about four times in five and loses the\nfinal at the first try about half the time. Turbo runs out in about one long break. A big hit should feel like an event,\nnot every tackle.\n\n---\n\n## 20. About & Credits screen and the exit interview\n\n- **About & Credits** (`about` scene, five pages at scale 1-2, L1/R1 or left/right, ✕ closes):\n  1. THUGBY TURBO: made with the my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (`E.versionLabel()`), the AI Hub session client 1.4.0; by\n     the model that built it; the title's RNG pick; \"an original game inspired by rugby; every team, person and place\n     is made up\".\n  2. SOURCE INFORMATION: Date 2026-11-03 17:48:28 · Source: rugby (over-the-top arcade style) · Plan: PLAN.md · Genre\n     and perspective · Tech · Art direction · Animation · Audio · Online · Testing · Research · Environment · Model ·\n     Usage (estimates only if available; \"unknown\" otherwise).\n  3. TESTING FEEDBACK (the four answers). 4. ENGINE FEEDBACK (the six answers, including the patches and why). 5. PROMPT\n     FEEDBACK (the four answers).\n  The builder writes these from the real build at the end (M9); \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed. The\n  same text goes in the final chat reply.\n- **`exit-interview.json`** in this folder, beside the HTML, in exactly TASK.md's shape; suggested `aiHub` values:\n  name \"THUGBY TURBO\", tagline \"Big hits, bigger hair, seven a side\", description \"Over-the-top arcade rugby sevens:\n  turbo runs, monster hits, a referee who only sees half of it, and a pub team's run at the Mega Cup.\", type \"Game\",\n  genre \"Sports\", source \"Rugby\", series \"\", players \"1–4\", controls \"Stick or WASD run, L1/R1 or Q/E pass, ✕ or Space\n  tackle and sidestep, ○ or C kick, R2 or Shift turbo, △ or R super\", tags `[\"sports\", \"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"3d\",\n  \"versus\", \"co-op\"]`. Check it parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n\n---\n\n## 21. Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `ThugbyTurbo-Rugby-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174828.html` in this folder plays from `file://` with no errors;\n      the dev subfolder holds the sources, tests and tools.\n- [ ] Every system in §7 works in play and is shown by the cup, the drills or the attract mode; nothing is stubbed; no\n      TODO or placeholder text anywhere (grep the sources for TODO, FIXME, TBD, lorem, placeholder).\n- [ ] Mega Cup (prologue, training, four matches, victory, third half, credits), Exhibition (any teams, venues,\n      weather, 1-4 players), Training Ground, Records, Settings, About & Credits all reachable and complete.\n- [ ] Controller-first 10-foot UI; PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox in Settings; keyboard and mouse native; prompts\n      follow the last device; touch-only screen with Settings; attract mode after 10 s, any input exits.\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu: live sliders for §14.2, reset to defaults, cheats, events, overlays, jumps.\n- [ ] All audio in code; babble voices for every speaker; music per scene with layers.\n- [ ] Local multiplayer 1-4; AI Hub shared-world passes the harness in all four configurations; outside a session the\n      game is unaffected.\n- [ ] `node test/run.mjs` passes, including the scripted playthrough; browser checks and screenshots reviewed.\n- [ ] Engine patches listed in `engine/PATCHES.md` and in Engine Feedback.\n- [ ] About & Credits pages and the chat reply carry Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback;\n      `exit-interview.json` parses.\n","numLines":75,"startLine":1600,"totalLines":1674}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AvDcpt1KenY4UYagYHiKFc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
